{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.SilverAnchorGrounding","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.SilverAnchorGrounding","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hoefsmit_bSq_eq_at_silver","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hoefsmit_bSq_eq_at_silver","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SilverAnchorGrounding.lean#L91-L99","doc":"**Hoefsmit `b² = 7/8` at the silver locus** (field form). Dividing the\ndivision-free identity `hoefsmit_bSq_numerator_silver` by the nonzero `(q²+1)²`\ngives the literal Hoefsmit ratio used by the silver-rung values. The denominator\nnonvanishing holds at `q = 1+√2` (there `q²+1 = 2+2√2 ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hoefsmit_bSq_numerator_silver","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hoefsmit_bSq_numerator_silver","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SilverAnchorGrounding.lean#L82-L89","doc":"**Hoefsmit `b²` numerator identity at the silver locus** (division-free,\ngeneric `CommRing`). With `b² = (q⁴ + q² + 1)/(q² + 1)²` (Hoefsmit), the relation\n`q² − 2q − 1 = 0` forces `8·(q⁴ + q² + 1) = 7·(q² + 1)²` — i.e. `b² = 7/8`. The\n`linear_combination` certificate is the cofactor `(q² + 2q − 1)` of\n`silver_quartic_factor`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.silver_quartic_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.silver_quartic_factor","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SilverAnchorGrounding.lean#L74-L80","doc":"**The defining factorisation** `q⁴ − 6q² + 1 = (q² − 2q − 1)(q² + 2q − 1)`:\nthe silver factor `q² − 2q − 1` and its bar-conjugate `q² + 2q − 1`. This is the\nalgebraic content behind the Hoefsmit `b²` identity below (it is the\n`linear_combination` cofactor). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.qA_numerator_zero_at_silver","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.qA_numerator_zero_at_silver","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SilverAnchorGrounding.lean#L65-L72","doc":"**The silver locus is the `Q_A` decay-prefactor zero.** The substrate-branch\n`Q_A` numerator factor `2q + 1 − q²` equals `−(q² − 2q − 1)`, so it vanishes\nexactly when `q` satisfies the silver relation `q² − 2q − 1 = 0`. This is where\n`F = Q_β/[Q_A·cos α_eff]` has its pole — the dominant `1/u_substrate`\ncharacteristic root of the `c_k` recurrence. ","signatureChunk":0}]}